          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pursuing+Stacks"} Pursuing Stacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"} Grothendieck
            introduced the idea of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/test+category"} test category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
          %h2#general General
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              %strong Cisinski model structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
                  are precisely the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              %li
                %p
                  it is a
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Since every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              structure.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Since every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adhesive+category"} adhesive category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
          #Localizer.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Say a class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \subset Mor(\mathcal{T})
              is an accessible
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localizer"} localizer
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              if it is a class of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
              in a Cisinski model structure on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \subset Mor(\mathcal{T})
              is contained in a smallest localizer, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Localizer"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\Sigma)
          %p
            One says that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\Sigma)
            is the localiser
            %em generated
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p So in particular a Cisinski model structure always exists.
          %h2#OnPresheafToposes On presheaf toposes
          %p
            We discuss how on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
            equipped with a suitable notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder+objects"} cylinder objects
            Cisinski model structures can be characterized fairly explicitly. After some
            %a{:href => "#PreliminaryNotions"} preliminaries
            %em
              , the main statement is theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureFromHomotopicalStructure"}
              below.
          %p
            (This follows sections 1.2 and 1.3 of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"} Cisinski 06
          %h3#PreliminaryNotions Preliminary notions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
