          .proof
            %h6#proof_15 Proof
            %p A bit of work…
          #CellularStructuresExist.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_12 Proposition
            %p
              There exists a cellular structure, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellularModel"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A)
            %p
              The set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              can be chosen to consist of morphisms into
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+objects"} quotient objects
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functors"} representables
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, prop. 1.2.27
            ), also sketched at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+model"} cellular model
          .proof
            %h6#proof_16 Proof
            %p
              Take in lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LemmaForGenerationOfMonos"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              to be the class of monomorphisms and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              to be the class of quotients of representables.
          #FirstFactorizationEstablishes.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              There exists a functorial factorization of morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A)
              into a monomorphism followed by an acyclic fibration.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, cor. 1.2.28
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_17 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PresheavesAreCompact"}
              every object is
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} small
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CellularStructuresExist"}
              we can apply the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
          %h5#AcyclicCofibrationFollowedByFibration Acyclic cofibration followed by fibration
          %p
            We show now for def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureMorphismsFromHomotopicalStructure"}
            that every morphism factors as an acyclic cofibration followed by a fibration. Since the fibrations are defined by right lifting against acylcic cofibrations, for this it is sufficient to establish a set of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} generating acyclic cofibrations
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsExist"}
            below. Establishing this takes a few technical lemmas.
          #FactorAnodyneFollowedByRLPAnodyne.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_4 Lemma
            %p Every morphism admits a factorization into an anodyne extension, followed by a morphism having the right lifting property against anodyne extensions.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, remark 1.3.29
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_18 Proof
            %p
              By the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PropertiesOfAnodyneExtensions"}
          #ElementaryJHomotopyIntoFibIsEquivRel.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_5 Lemma
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in PSh(A)
              is fibrant, then for any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \in PSh(A)
              elementary
              = succeed "-homotopy," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ElementaryJHomotopy"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{PSh(A)}(K,T)
              and coincides with
              = succeed "-homotopy." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, lemma 1.3.30
            ).
          #EveryAnodyneExtensionIsWeakEquivalence.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_13 Proposition
            %p Every anodyne extension is a weak equivalence.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, lemma 1.3.31
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_19 Proof
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo :
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j : K \to L
              an anodyne extension and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              a fibrant object, we need to show that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ho
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Ho
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Ho
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ho_J(j,T) :  Ho_J(L,T) \to Ho_J(K,T)
            %p is a bijection.
            %p
              It is surjective by the defining lifting property, which provides
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi j
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi σ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    K &amp;\stackrel{}{\to}&amp; T
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{j}}
                    \&amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\sigma}}
                    \\\
                    L
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              To see injectivity, let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi l
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi l
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_0, l_1 : L \to T
              be two morphisms such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi l
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_0 \circ j
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi l
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_1 \circ j
              coincide in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ho
                        %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_J
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ElementaryJHomotopyIntoFibIsEquivRel"}
              this is the case precisely if there is an elementary
              = succeed "-homotopy" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : I \otimes K \to T
              relating them. This induces the horizontal morphism in the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi I
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi I
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi L
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi h
                                %mo ,
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %msub
                                  %mi l
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo ,
                                %msub
                                  %mi l
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi η
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi I
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi L
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    (I \otimes K) \cup ((\partial I) \otimes L)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{(h,(l_0,l_1))}{\to}&amp;
                    T
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\eta}}
                    \\\
                    I \otimes L
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the left morphism is anodyne, by the second clause of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AnodyneExtensions"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi η
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta
              exists. This lift exhibits a
              = succeed "-homotopy" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi l
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ⇒
                      %msub
                        %mi l
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_0 \Rightarrow l_1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi l
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_0
              was already equal to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi l
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_1
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ho
                        %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi j
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j^*
              is injective.
          #WeakEquivalencesBetweenFibrantObjects.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_6 Lemma
            %p
              A morphism between fibrant objects is a weak equivalence precisely if it is a
              = succeed "-homotopy" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JHomotopyEquivalence"}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, lemma 1.3.32
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_20 Proof
            %p
              Is is clear that every
              = succeed "-homotopy" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              be a weak equivalence between fibrant objects. Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ho
                      %mi J
                      %mi fib
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Ho
                      %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_J^{fib} \hookrightarrow Ho_J
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ho
                        %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_J
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#JHomotopyEquivalence"}
              on the fibrant objects. The localization
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(f)
              is by definition in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ho
                      %mi J
                      %mi fib
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_J^{fib}
              and for all objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ho
                      %mi J
                      %mi fib
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \in Ho_J^{fib}
              the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ho
                      %mi J
                      %mi fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_J^{fib}(Q(f), T)
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(f)
              itself is an isomorphism in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Ho
                        %mi J
                        %mi fib
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_J^{fib}
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ho
                        %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_J
          #NaiveFibAndDualStrongDefRetractIsAcyclFib.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_7 Lemma
            %p
              If a morphism has the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
              against the anodyne extensions, then it is an acyclic fibration precisely if it is a dual
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+deformation+retract"} strong deformation retract
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, lemma 1.3.33
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_21 Proof
            %p
              That the former implies the latter was the statement of lemma
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SectionsOfAcyclicFibrationsAreDefRetracts"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              be a dual strong deformation retract, meaning that there is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s : Y \to X
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %mi id
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \circ s = id
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k : I \otimes X \to X
              exhibiting a
              = succeed "-homotopy" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi id
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id \Rightarrow s \circ p
              %em strong
              means that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mi p
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \circ k = p \circ \sigma_X
            %p We need to show that this implies for
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi K
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi i
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi p
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi L
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi b
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    K &amp;\stackrel{a}{\to}&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{i}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{p}}
                    \\\
                    L &amp;\stackrel{b}{\to}&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              a commuting diagram with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              a monomorphism, there is a lift. To this end, observe that the given structures induce a morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi I
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (I \otimes K) \cup (\{1\} \otimes L) \to X
            %p such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi I
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi K
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∪
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
