          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
            %p A cofibration into a fibrant object is a weak equivalence precisely if it is an anodyne extension.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, cor 1.3.35
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_23 Proof
            %p
              By lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EveryAnodyneExtensionIsWeakEquivalence"}
              we already know that every anodyne extension is a weak equivalence. So we need to show that a cofibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : A \to T
              into a fibrant object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              which is a weak equivalence is also an anodyne extension. By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FactorAnodyneFollowedByRLPAnodyne"}
              we may factor this as
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi q
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i = q \circ j
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              an anodyne extension and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              having RLP against anodyne extensions. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
              is a weak equivalence, by 2-out-of-3 so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NaiveFibIntoFibIsWeakEquivIffItIsAcyclicFib"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              is an acyclic fibration.
            %p
              Therefore we have a lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              in
