                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi K
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \cap K  \to K
              soit une cofibration triviale.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, prop. 1.3.40
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_25 Proof
            %p Three pages of work…
          #GeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsExist.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_16 Proposition
            %p There exists a set of generating acyclic cofibrations.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, prop. 1.3.42
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_26 Proof
            %p
              Use lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LemmaForGenerationOfMonos"}
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              the class of acyclic cofibrations and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Acc
                      %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = Acc_\alpha(A)
              the set of
              = succeed "-accessible" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
          #FactorizationAcyclicCofibFib.num_cor
            %h6#corollary_4 Corollary
            %p There is a functorial factorization of every morphism into an acyclic cofibration followed by a fibration.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, cor. 1.3.43
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof_27 Proof
            %p
              By prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneratingAcyclicCofibrationsExist"}
              and prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PresheavesAreCompact"}
              we may apply the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object+argument"} small object argument
          %h4#Completeness Completeness
          %p
            We list lemmas to show prop.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConditionsForCompleteness"}
          %p (…)
          %h3#ALocalizers Localizers
          %p
            Continuing to let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A)
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
          #ALocalizer.num_defn
            %h6#definition_16 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                \-localizer
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              of morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \subset Mor(PSh(A))
              satisfying the following axioms
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3"}> 2-out-of-3
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  every acyclic fibration, def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AcyclicFibration"}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              %li
                %p
                  The class of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
                  that is in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  is stable under
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                  and
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
            %p
              The elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              we call
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  \-equivalences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Mor
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(PSh(A))
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              of morphisms, the smallest
              = succeed "-localizer" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is called the
              = succeed "-localized" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %strong generated
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              = succeed "-localizer" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
              = succeed "." do
                %strong accessible
              %strong
                minimal
                = succeed "-localizer" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\emptyset)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, def. 1.4.1
            ))
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_17 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi J
                    %mo ,
                    %mi AnExt
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J,AnExt)
              a homotopical structure, def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopicalStructure"}
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              of weak equivalences of the induced model category structure of theorem
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureFromHomotopicalStructure"}
              is an
              = succeed "-localizer." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
              is a small set generating the anodyne extensions,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi AnExt
                      %mo =
                      %mi LLP
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi RLP
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AnExt = LLP(RLP(\Lambda))
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo =
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Λ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W = W(\Lambda)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, prop. 1.4.2
            ))
          %p
          #TheoremCharacterisationOfAccessibleLocalisersForPresheafCategories.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \subset Mor(PSh(A))
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  is an accessible
                  = succeed "-localizer," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ALocalizer"}
              %li
                %p
                  There is a set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi Mor
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \subset Mor(PSh(A))
                  of monomorphisms, such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  is the class of weak equivalences of the model structure induced by theorem
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureFromHomotopicalStructure"}
                  from the homotopical structure, def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopicalStructure"}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+cylinder"} Lawvere cylinder
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LawvereCylinder"}
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi AnExt
                          %mo :
                          %mo =
                          %mi S
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} AnExt := S
              %li
                %p
                  There is some homotopical structure, def.
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopicalStructure"}
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi PSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  is the class of weak equivalences of the model structure corresponding to it by theorem
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ModelStructureFromHomotopicalStructure"}
              %li
                %p
                  There exists a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A)
                  such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
                  is its class of weak equivalences, and such that the cofibrations are the monomorphisms.
            %p
              In particular,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A)
              admits a model structure whose cofibrations are the monomorphisms and whose weak equivalences are the minimal localizer,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\emptyset)
              %strong minimal model structure
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi PSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A)
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LawvereCylinder"}
              and the empty set.
            %p
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, theorem 1.4.3
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              This may be compared to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeff+Smith%27s+theorem"} Jeff Smith's theorem
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, scholie 1.4.6
            ))
          %h3#SimplicialCompletion Simplicial completion
          %p
            Give a localizer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi horiz
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_{horiz}
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(A \times \Delta)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi horiz
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  W_{horiz} \coloneqq
                  \\{
                  X \times q^* (\Delta_1) \to X
                  \\}
                  \\,.
          %p (…)
          %p
            See (
            %a{:href => "#Ara"}> Ara, p. 9
            ).
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The archetypical and motivating example is the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
                over the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
                (
                %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"}> Cisinski 06, section 2
                ).
            %li
              %p
                Accordingly, the
                %em injective
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
                over a site
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a Cisinski model structure, namely on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C \times \Delta)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} left Bousfield localization
                of such a model structure is still a Cisinski model structure, since left Bousfield localization preserves the class of cofibrations.
              %p
                Notice that, as discussed there, every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentable (infinity,1)-category
                has a presentation by such a localization, hence by a Cisinski model structure.
            %li
              %p
                Also the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+quasi-categories"} model structure for quasi-categories
                is a Cisinski model structure on
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"} spine
                inclusions.
              %p
                Moreover, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+complete+Segal+spaces"} model structure for complete Segal spaces
                is the
                %a{:href => "#SimplicialCompletion"} simplicial completion
                of this model structure. (see
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Ara"} Ara
            %li
              %p
                As a
                = succeed "-variant" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+set"} cellular set
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+cellular+sets"} model structure on cellular sets
                is a Cisinski model structure on the category of presheaves over the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+category"} Theta category
                restricted to
                = succeed "-cells." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dendroidal+sets"} model structure on dendroidal sets
                is not exactly a Cisinki model structure, but is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred
                from one that is.
            %li
              %p
                For any small category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DefinitionHomotopicalDatum"}
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi J
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ∅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (J, \emptyset)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi J
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                is the
                = succeed "(Definition" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+cylinder"} Lawvere cylinder
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LawvereCylinder"}
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "#Cisinski06"} Cisinski 06, rem. 1.3.15
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Ω
                      %msub
                        %mo ∪
                        %mi A
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times \Omega \cup_A B \to B \times \Omega
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
                are generators for the class of monomorphisms. This is sometimes known as the
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    minimal Cisinski model structure
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/minimal+Cisinski+model+structure"} ?
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheoremCharacterisationOfAccessibleLocalisersForPresheafCategories"}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#properness Properness
          #RightProper.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\Sigma)
              is the localizer generated by a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              in a Grothendieck topos, then (the Cisinski model structure whose weak equivalences are)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\Sigma)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+proper+model+category"} right proper
              if and only if pullback along fibrations between fibrant objects in this model structure takes morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              to weak equivalences.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Cisinski02"} Cisinski 02, Théorème 4.8
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+model+category#FibrationsBetweenFibrantObjectsSuffice"} this proposition
          %p
            We can use this to prove that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally presentable (∞,1)-category
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally cartesian closed (∞,1)-category
            if and only if it has a presentation by a right proper Cisinski model structure. See
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} locally cartesian closed (∞,1)-category
            for details.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/test+topos"} test topos
          %h2#References References
          %p The original articles are
          %ul
            %li#Cisinski02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"} Denis-Charles Cisinski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Théories homotopiques dans les topos
            %li#Cisinski06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Les préfaisceaux comme types d’homotopie
                %strong 308
                Soc. Math. France (2006), 392 pages &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=AST_2006__308__R1_0"} numdam:AST_2006__308__R1_0
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.univ-toulouse.fr/~dcisinsk/ast.pdf"} pdf
          %p A more recent, English presentation of much of this material appears in section 2.4 of
          %ul
            %li#Cisinski20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              %em Higher category theory and homotopical algebra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.uni-regensburg.de/cisinski/CatLR.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A textbook account:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Garth+Warner"}> Garth Warner
              ,
              %em Homotopical Topos Theory
              (2012) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://sites.math.washington.edu//~warner/HTT_Warner.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Waner-HomotopicalTopos.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Further developments:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rick+Jardine"}> Rick Jardine
                ,
                %em Categorical homotopy theory
                (2003) (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0669/"}> K-theory
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marc+Olschok"}> Marc Olschok
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On constructions of left determined model structures
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://is.muni.cz/th/183259/prif_d/diss.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Henry"}> Simon Henry
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Minimal model structures
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2011.13408"} arXiv:2011.13408
          %p Some work on generalizing from presheaf toposes to all toposes is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              %em Faisceaux localement asphériques
              (preliminary version), 2003,
              %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.uni-regensburg.de/cisinski/mtest2.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also
          %ul#Ara
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"}> André Joyal
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/joyalscatlab/published/Cisinski%27s+theory"} Cisinski's theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dimitri+Ara"}> Dimitri Ara
                ,
                %em Higher quasi-categories vs higher Rezk spaces
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.4354"}> arXiv:1206.4354
                )
